'He ordains me, He describes me, I am to be prescribed, I am to be excluded' — thus;
the heart of this [scripture], directly, no one other than Me knows.
Thus in the <s>Bhāgavata</s>.
// 4 //

'<s>Bhagavān</s>' is called by the words 'ananta' (infinite), '<s>Brahman</s>,' 'ānanda' (bliss), and the like;
<s>Viṣṇu</s> alone is [so] proclaimed primarily; for others, [these words are used] figuratively.
Thus in the <s>Brāhma</s> [Purāṇa].

But this is not so.
Because <s>Viṣṇu</s> alone is <s>Prāṇa</s>; for the same reason — '<s>Śrī</s> and <s>Lakṣmī</s> are Your consorts;
day and night are Your sides' (<s>Taittirīya Āraṇyaka</s> 3.13) — because of such marks of His [alone]. //

'He, splitting open this very boundary, entered by this door' (<s>Aitareya Āraṇyaka</s> 2.4.3);
